{title: Divide and Scatter}
{subtitle: Genesis 29:34; 34:25–31; 46:11; 49:5–7; Exodus 6:16–20}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
She bore [C]three [Gm]sons to join her [Dm]heart
Now at last my husband [C]stays
Named [Gm]Levi for the bond [Dm]they share
The third son of Jacob's days
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Sime[C]on [Gm]and Levi took their swords
A[Dm]gainst the unsuspecting city
Killing [C]ev[Gm]ery male in the crowd
Taking [Dm]Dinah from the pit
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Cursed be their [C]anger so fierce
[Gm]And their fury is [Bb]cruel
I will divide [C]them in Jacob
And scatter them [Dm]in Israel
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Jacob warned of the [C]stench they bring
[Gm]To the Canaanites and [Dm]Perizzites
My men are few and [C]few are [Gm]friends
If they attack our house[Dm]holds' sites
They seized the flocks and the [C]herds
[Gm]And the donkeys in the [Dm]field
Took the children and the [C]wives
[Gm]And the wealth of every [Dm]shield
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Cursed be their anger so fierce
[C]And their fury is [Gm]cruel
I will di[Bb]vide them in Jacob
[C]And scatter them in Is[Dm]rael
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Sons of Levi are [C]Gershon
[Gm]Kohath and Mera[Dm]ri
Levi lived one hundred thir-ty-sev-[C]en
[Gm]Years in the land that was [Dm]dry
Amram took his sister Joche[Gm]bed
Bearing Aaron and [Dm]Moses
Kohath lived one hundred thir-ty-three [C]
[Gm]In this strange and foreign [Dm]house
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Cursed be their anger so fierce
[C]And their fury [Gm]is cruel
I will [Bb]divide them in Ja[C]cob
And scatter them in Is[Dm]rael
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Scattered in [C]Jacob
Divided in Is[Dm]rael
{end_of_verse}
